Z||000003||mshill||01-26-2000||12:23 AM||||A little off topic, but it reminds me of when my dad (64 at the time) was out on the boat with us and my 9 and 11 year old sons just finished a couple pulls on a kneeboard.  They made it look so easy that my dad (in very good shape for 64) asked if I thought he could give it a try.  I said sure (I have always considered my father to be quite strong and coordinated).  Well, he got out there and couldn't get up, and if you know kneeboards, they tend to bounce if you don't get on top of them quickly.  He ended up banging his head on the board and came into the boat bleeding.  I really felt bad about it. He won't be doing any behind-the-boat water sports with us again.<BR>||||reg||9
